    <string name="settings_advanced_m2_note">M2 note: switching to Advanced enables no new capability — zero permission requests, zero Runtime installs, zero Root sessions, zero new network endpoints. Each advanced capability is enabled by its own later milestone, scoped and immediately revocable.</string>
    <string name="settings_consumer_standard_only">This build offers only the Standard profile; there is no Advanced entry (the consumer channel has no Standard → Advanced path, ADR-0005/0006).</string>
    <string name="settings_advanced_confirm_title">Switch to Advanced — risk notice</string>
    <string name="settings_advanced_confirm_ok">I understand, confirm switch</string>
    <string name="profile_advanced_risk_summary">Switching to Advanced itself grants no capability: it requests no system permission, installs no Runtime, requests no Root, connects to no new network endpoint, and widens no available tools.\n\nAdvanced opens controlled advanced capabilities (All-files, Accessibility, offline PRoot, Root, precise LAN origin, and so on). Each capability still must be enabled individually, scoped, and can be revoked immediately; no advanced capability is enabled in the current version.\n\nThe shared security core is unchanged: the model cannot self-authorize; schema validation, Policy, per-use approval, audit and revocation rules are never disabled or downgraded under Advanced.</string>

